<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/torus.rs. std only, integer arithmetic, no panics on constructor input. Torus::new(side_lengths:&[usize])->Option<Self>: None if empty, any side<2, or site count overflows. Stable index conventions, stated in the module doc comment and relied on by other modules and future GPU code: site index = sum c_i*stride_i (stride_0=1); link index = site*d+direction; plane index of first<second lexicographic (0,1),(0,2),...; plaquette index = site*plane_count+plane_index. Methods: dimension, side_lengths, site_count, plane_count, link_count, plaquette_count, cube_count, site_index (coordinates reduced mod sides), site_coordinate, site_coordinates, neighbor(site,direction,forward) with periodic wrap, link_index, plane_index, plane_directions (inverse), plaquette_index, plaquette_links (order of the Wilson plaquette variable U(y,mu)U(y+e_mu,nu)U(y+e_nu,mu)^-1U(y,nu)^-1), link_coboundary (the 2(d-1) plaquettes containing a link), cube_plaquettes (six faces), cubes. Independent tests: tests/geometry.rs (cell counts, round trips, incidence double counting, delta delta = 0, GF(2) rank = dV-V+1-d, degenerate inputs rejected).
